# Local sibling-package path wiring (dev only). Absolute paths on purpose: this file
# is machine-local by definition, and a relative `../magic` does not resolve from a
# worktree under .claude/worktrees/. Measured: a verbatim copy there fails version
# solving; with absolute paths `flutter pub get` and `flutter analyze` both pass.
# `.worktreeinclude` copies it into every worktree Claude creates.
pubspec_overrides.yaml

# Worktrees Claude Code creates for parallel sessions and isolated subagents.
#
# They sit inside the working tree rather than beside it. `git clean -xdf` leaves them
# alone: git's nested-repository guard resolves a gitfile too, so it reports "Skipping
# repository .claude/worktrees/<slug>" and the contents survive. `git clean -xdff` does
# not skip them, and wipes a live worktree while `.git/worktrees/<slug>` survives,
# leaving a registration that `git worktree prune` then has to clear.
.claude/worktrees/

# Secrets (never commit; .env.example is the template)

# ac orchestration artifacts (plan + evidence)
.ac/

# Local QA report (not part of the published example)
/REPORT.md

# pubspec.lock IS committed here, unlike the magic_example template this was
# forked from. That template could not commit one: it is forked, and its lock
# could only ever be generated with pubspec_overrides.yaml active, so it always
# encoded `path: "../magic"` and friends. Depools is the application, not the
# template, and an application needs a lock or a deploy is not reproducible.
#
# The catch that reasoning was protecting against is real and still applies: a
# lock generated while pubspec_overrides.yaml is active encodes local sibling
# paths that exist on no CI runner or deploy host. So the committed lock must be
# the hosted-only one, regenerated with the overrides moved aside:
#
#   mv pubspec_overrides.yaml /tmp/ && flutter pub get && git add pubspec.lock
#   mv /tmp/pubspec_overrides.yaml .
#
# `bin/check` fails when the lock contains a local path, so a wrong one cannot be
# committed by accident. Day-to-day local `pub get` runs will dirty the lock with
# paths; leave those unstaged.

